<mujoco model="ur5e_pendulum_attachment">
  <!--
  Standalone MJCF for the physical "UR5e Pendulum v1" apparatus
  (cartpole_cad/UR5e Pendulum v1.zip) -- the free-swinging "pole" this
  workspace's original "real_Cartpole" name refers to, mounted at the
  UR5e's wrist_3 attachment_site via an OnRobot tool-changer.

  Meant to be composed onto the existing, PROTECTED centerpiece model
  (assets/ur5e_torque/ur5e_torque.xml, see AGENTS.md sec 2 -- "never
  delete or silently regenerate it") via mujoco.MjSpec.attach(site=...)
  at that model's "attachment_site" -- see
  simulation/ur5e_pendulum_compose.py for the loader. This file is NEVER
  included via plain <include> into ur5e_torque.xml or its scene.xml;
  it has no <worldbody> root itself so it cannot be loaded standalone as
  a top-level model (this is intentional -- it is an attachment
  fragment, not a scene).

  ============================================================
  DIMENSION PROVENANCE -- read before trusting any number below
  ============================================================
  The CAD (cartpole_cad/UR5e Pendulum v1.zip) is a genuine SolidWorks
  assembly (UR5e Pendulum v1.SLDASM) with real custom parts (Pendulum
  Rod, Rod Housing, Shaft Housing, Sensor Housing, Linear Motion Rod,
  8mm Bore Clamp) plus catalog hardware (McMaster fasteners, an MF128ZZ
  flanged ball bearing) and a CUI/Same Sky AMT222B-8000-S single-turn
  absolute magnetic encoder assembly. SolidWorks .SLDPRT/.SLDASM files
  are a proprietary binary format this environment has no reader for
  (no SolidWorks, no working translator found -- cadquery/OCP was
  installed and DOES read the two open-format .STEP files in the
  archive, but not the native SolidWorks parts).

  What is REAL (extracted or directly inferred from the archive):
    - OnRobot tool-changer robot-side plate: 71mm x 71mm x 16.1mm
      (bounding box, read via cadquery from
      "ST-RB-028-0004 OnRobot Tool Changer (Robot Side).STEP").
    - Tool-side plate bounding box: 75.51mm x 28.40mm x 71.00mm (same
      method, "...0023...Tool Side.STEP").
    - Rod/shaft diameter = 8mm -- not measured, but two independently
      named parts in the archive reference "8mm" explicitly ("8mm Bore
      Clamp", "Same_Sky_AMT-Sleeve-REV-D(8 mm)"), a real, non-arbitrary
      signal for this one dimension.
    - The encoder is a SINGLE-TURN ABSOLUTE type (CUI/Same Sky AMT22
      series) -- confirmed by part family, exact bit-resolution not
      confirmed (the "-8000-S" suffix was not decoded with confidence,
      not asserted here).

  What is PLACEHOLDER (physically reasonable, NOT measured -- flagged
  explicitly on every such value below, must be corrected against the
  real CAD/hardware before this model is used for anything beyond a
  first smoke test):
    - Pendulum rod LENGTH (0.30 m assumed -- a common lab-scale choice,
      no support from the archive's file list or metadata).
    - Rod/housing MASS and material density (assumed mild steel,
      7850 kg/m^3, since "Linear Motion Rod" + a ball-bearing pivot
      reads as a hardened-steel linear/rotary shaft component, but
      this is an inference, not a measurement).
    - Pivot joint AXIS ORIENTATION relative to attachment_site -- chosen
      here so the rod hangs down under gravity from a horizontal start
      in this file's own smoke test (tools/diagnostics/
      ur5e_pendulum_smoke_test.py), NOT derived from the CAD assembly's
      actual mate definitions (which are unreadable). If the real
      mechanism's swing plane differs, this needs correcting.
    - No discrete "bob" end-mass is modeled -- the archive's part list
      has no separate weighted part beyond the rod/housings, so mass is
      modeled as distributed along a uniform rod plus a small lumped
      mass for the encoder/housing cluster near the pivot. If the real
      assembly has a separate end weight, this is wrong and needs a
      dedicated body added.

  Do not treat any PLACEHOLDER value as ground truth for anything beyond
  a first-pass kinematic/dynamic sanity check.
  -->

  <default>
    <default class="pendulum">
      <joint damping="0.02" frictionloss="0.01"/>
      <geom contype="0" conaffinity="0" density="7850"/>
    </default>
  </default>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="pendulum_mount" pos="0 0 0">
      <!-- OnRobot tool-changer stack: REAL bounding-box dimensions
           (see provenance note above). Modeled as a simple flanged
           cylinder pair, not the real tool-changer geometry (STEP
           files were read for bounding box only, not full mesh
           extraction -- a real mesh import is a follow-up, not done
           here). -->
      <geom name="toolchanger_robot_side" type="cylinder" size="0.0355 0.00805" class="pendulum" rgba="0.35 0.35 0.38 1"/>
      <geom name="toolchanger_tool_side" type="cylinder" size="0.0355 0.0355" pos="0 0 0.0355" class="pendulum" rgba="0.3 0.3 0.32 1"/>

      <!-- Encoder/sensor housing cluster (Shaft Housing + Sensor Housing
           + AMT222 assembly), lumped as one small mass near the pivot.
           PLACEHOLDER mass (0.06 kg) -- order-of-magnitude guess for a
           small encoder + housing stack, not a measured value. -->
      <body name="pendulum_hub" pos="0 0 0.071">
        <geom name="pendulum_hub_geom" type="cylinder" size="0.020 0.015" class="pendulum" rgba="0.15 0.15 0.18 1" mass="0.06"/>

        <!-- The single swing DOF -- represents the AMT222 absolute
             encoder's measured axis. Axis choice is a PLACEHOLDER (see
             provenance note); tuned only so the rod hangs under gravity
             in this file's own smoke test, not derived from the real
             assembly's mate geometry. -->
        <joint name="pendulum_hinge" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" pos="0 0 0" class="pendulum" range="-3.14159 3.14159" limited="false"/>
        <site name="pendulum_hinge_site" pos="0 0 0" size="0.004" rgba="1 0 0 1"/>

        <!-- Pendulum rod: 8mm diameter is a real, archive-supported
             value; 0.30m length and steel density are PLACEHOLDERS
             (see provenance note). Rod extends along local -Z from the
             pivot; mass computed from density x volume by the compiler
             (no explicit mass override), consistent with the
             class="pendulum" default density above. -->
        <body name="pendulum_rod" pos="0 0 0">
          <geom name="pendulum_rod_geom" type="cylinder" fromto="0 0 0  0 0 -0.30" size="0.004" class="pendulum" rgba="0.6 0.6 0.65 1"/>
          <site name="pendulum_tip_site" pos="0 0 -0.30" size="0.006" rgba="0 1 0 1"/>
        </body>
      </body>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <sensor>
    <!-- Mirrors the real AMT222's role: a single-axis absolute angle
         reading of pendulum_hinge. jointpos on a hinge joint returns
         the joint's own signed angle in radians -- this is the
         simulated equivalent of what the real encoder reports over its
         digital interface (exact resolution/interface not modeled). -->
    <jointpos name="pendulum_angle_sensor" joint="pendulum_hinge"/>
  </sensor>
</mujoco>
